GENS: the frequency counter that wraps is unsigned

Fcnt is the phase of a slot: the frequency step Finc is added to it for every
sample, and it is meant to run off the end and carry on from the other side.
It is an int, and the overflow of a signed int is undefined behaviour, so
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer stops the program the first time a slot's phase
comes round, about a second into a note:

  src/chips/gens/Ym2612.cpp:1411:3: runtime error: signed integer overflow:
  2147217408 + 1065088 cannot be represented in type 'int'

An unsigned int says what the counter is: wrapping is what it does, and it is
defined. The field is only ever set to zero, added to (in UPDATE_PHASE and
both halves of UPDATE_PHASE_LFO, twelve places in all) and read into the int
that GET_CURRENT_PHASE() keeps, where the phase is shifted right and masked;
the mask leaves the same bits as before, so the sound does not change.

This is ADLplug-Next's own patch, applied to the submodule by
cmake/Patches.cmake when CMake configures, and it goes away once the change is
upstream.

diff --git a/src/chips/gens/Ym2612_p.hpp b/src/chips/gens/Ym2612_p.hpp
index 2b5dd65..bcb738e 100644
--- a/src/chips/gens/Ym2612_p.hpp
+++ b/src/chips/gens/Ym2612_p.hpp
@@ -67,7 +67,7 @@ class Ym2612Private
 			unsigned int *DR; // Decay Rate (table pointeur) = Taux pour la régression (DR[KSR])
 			unsigned int *SR; // Sustin Rate (table pointeur) = Taux pour le maintien (SR[KSR])
 			unsigned int *RR; // Release Rate (table pointeur) = Taux pour le relâchement (RR[KSR])
-			int Fcnt;	// Frequency Count = compteur-fréquence pour déterminer l'amplitude actuelle (SIN[Finc >> 16])
+			unsigned int Fcnt;	// Frequency Count = compteur-fréquence pour déterminer l'amplitude actuelle (SIN[Finc >> 16])
 			int Finc;	// frequency step = pas d'incrémentation du compteur-fréquence
 						// plus le pas est grand, plus la fréquence est aïgu (ou haute)
 			int Ecurp;	// Envelope current phase = cette variable permet de savoir dans quelle phase
